  <DocRow class="dr-section">
    <h2 id="ci-notify">Notify a stream from CI</h2>
    <p>
      A build or deploy script can post into a channel. Give the message a stable
      <code>clientMessageId</code> so a retried pipeline step never double-posts.
      First find a stream to post into:
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      slot="code"
      lang="bash"
      label="List channels"
      code={`curl "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/streams?type=channel&limit=20" \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}"`}
      run={{ method: "GET", path: "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/streams?type=channel&limit=20" }}
    />
  </DocRow>

  <DocRow>
    <p>Then post, reusing the same ID across retries:</p>
    <Fragment slot="code">
      <CodeBlock
        lang="bash"
        label="Post once"
        code={`curl -X POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/streams/STREAM_ID/messages \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}" \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\
  -d '{
    "content": "**Deploy:** v2.4.1 shipped to production. :rocket:",
    "clientMessageId": "ci-deploy-2.4.1"
  }'`}
